          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "convert-an-asciidoc-document-to-pdf",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Convert an AsciiDoc document to PDF"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In addition to the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "asciidoctor-pdf"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " command, you can convert to PDF using the Asciidoctor API. The selection of the Asciidoctor PDF converter is controlled through use of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "backend"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " keyword, which may be specified either as an API option or a document attribute."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "First, make sure you have the Asciidoctor PDF gem installed and available on the Ruby runtime path. Once that step is complete, require the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "asciidoctor-pdf"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " gem to load the Asciidoctor PDF converter."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "require 'asciidoctor-pdf'"
              }
            ],
            "language": "ruby",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can now use the main Asciidoctor API to convert an AsciiDoc document to PDF."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "require 'asciidoctor-pdf'\n\nAsciidoctor.convert_file 'basic-example.adoc', backend: 'pdf', safe: :unsafe"
              }
            ],
            "language": "ruby",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This API call is equivalent to the command shown in the previous section. The script first requires the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "asciidoctor-pdf"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " gem (equivalent to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "-r asciidoctor-pdf"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). Then it invokes Asciidoctor with the safe mode set to unsafe (equivalent to the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "asciidoctor"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " command) and the backend to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "pdf"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (equivalent to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "-b pdf"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). You can run this script using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ruby"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " command."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When the script completes, you should see the file "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "basic-example.pdf"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": [
                  "path"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in the current directory. You can use the typical set of API options to customize where this file is written."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "convert"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method instead of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "convert_file"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method, Asciidoctor will return the instance of the converter (which is also an instance of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Prawn::Document"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). If you want to capture the PDF stream, you need to do so by redirecting the output to a StringIO object."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "require 'asciidoctor-pdf'\nrequire 'stringio'\n\nAsciidoctor.convert 'I *love* AsciiDoc!', backend: 'pdf', safe: :unsafe, to_file: (pdf = StringIO.new)\nputs pdf.string"
              }
            ],
            "language": "ruby",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can also capture the PDF strea after the fact by passing the returned document to the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "write"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method on that same object."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "require 'asciidoctor-pdf'\nrequire 'stringio'\n\ndoc = Asciidoctor.convert 'I *love* AsciiDoc!', backend: 'pdf', safe: :unsafe\ndoc.write doc, (pdf = StringIO.new)\nputs pdf.string"
              }
            ],
            "language": "ruby",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This call is the equivalent to the following:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "require 'asciidoctor-pdf'\nrequire 'stringio'\n\nputs (Asciidoctor.convert 'I *love* AsciiDoc!', backend: 'pdf', safe: :unsafe).render"
              }
            ],
            "language": "ruby",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The main difference is that calling "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "render"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " directly on the returned converter object does not trigger the cleanup routine, which is important when converting to PDF. Thus, using a StringIO object as the target is preferable."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "convert-to-pdf-using-the-api",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Convert to PDF using the API"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Convert AsciiDoc to PDF"
      }
    ]
  }
}
